Feature: Validate and compare data between product_plant and product_plant_v2 tables, generating a pp_validation_results table with column-wise match/mismatch indicators.

  Background:
    Given the source table purgo_playground.product_plant exists with columns:
      | plant_id | plant_cd | company_cd | source_system_cd | product_line | primary_uom_cd | global_uom_conversion_rate | global_uom_cd | lifecycle_status | flais_active | sales_rank_abc | inventory_rank_abc | make_buy |
    And the target table purgo_playground.product_plant_v2 exists with columns:
      | plant_id | plant_cd | company_cd | source_system_cd | product_line | primary_uom_cd | global_uom_conversion_rate | global_uom_cd | lifecycle_status | flais_active | sales_rank_abc | inventory_rank_abc | make_buy |
    And the output table purgo_playground.pp_validation_results will be dropped and recreated before each run
    And all columns from both tables will be aliased as _src and _tgt respectively in the output table
    And the output table will have columns in the order: src column, tgt column, validation column for each field
    And the join key for comparison is plant_id
    And null values are considered a match only if both source and target are null
    And decimal/float values are compared with precision up to one decimal place (e.g., 1.0 == 1.00)
    And if a row exists in one table but not the other, missing_from_src or missing_from_tgt will be set to 'Y' and all validation columns will be 'Mismatch'
    And duplicate plant_id values in either table will result in an error and log the error_message field
    And the output table will be overwritten on each run (not appended or partitioned)
    And the script is expected to run once per data refresh

  Scenario Outline: Validate matching rows between product_plant and product_plant_v2
    Given a row exists in product_plant with plant_id = <plant_id_src> and in product_plant_v2 with plant_id = <plant_id_tgt>
    When the script compares each column value between product_plant and product_plant_v2 for the given plant_id
    Then the output table pp_validation_results will contain:
      | plant_id_src | plant_id_tgt | plant_id_validation | plant_cd_src | plant_cd_tgt | plant_cd_validation | company_cd_src | company_cd_tgt | company_cd_validation | source_system_cd_src | source_system_cd_tgt | source_system_cd_validation | product_line_src | product_line_tgt | product_line_validation | primary_uom_cd_src | primary_uom_cd_tgt | primary_uom_cd_validation | global_uom_conversion_rate_src | global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt | global_uom_conversion_rate_validation | global_uom_cd_src | global_uom_cd_tgt | global_uom_cd_validation | lifecycle_status_src | lifecycle_status_tgt | lifecycle_status_validation | flais_active_src | flais_active_tgt | flais_active_validation | sales_rank_abc_src | sales_rank_abc_tgt | sales_rank_abc_validation | inventory_rank_abc_src | inventory_rank_abc_tgt | inventory_rank_abc_validation | make_buy_src | make_buy_tgt | make_buy_validation | missing_from_src | missing_from_tgt | error_message |
