  Scenario: Handle duplicate plant_id in either table
    Given product_plant contains duplicate plant_id values
    When the script processes the comparison
    Then the output table pp_validation_results will contain an error_message "Duplicate plant_id found in product_plant" for the affected plant_id rows

    Given product_plant_v2 contains duplicate plant_id values
    When the script processes the comparison
    Then the output table pp_validation_results will contain an error_message "Duplicate plant_id found in product_plant_v2" for the affected plant_id rows

  Scenario Outline: Validate null handling and decimal precision
    Given a row exists in both tables with plant_id = <plant_id>
    When the script compares global_uom_conversion_rate_src and global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt
    Then global_uom_conversion_rate_validation is <expected_validation>

    Examples:
      | plant_id | global_uom_conversion_rate_src | global_uom_conversion_rate_tgt | expected_validation |
      | 401      | 1.0                           | 1.00                          | Match              |
      | 402      | 2.5                           | 2.50                          | Match              |
      | 403      | null                          | null                          | Match              |
      | 404      | 3.0                           | 3.1                           | Mismatch           |
      | 405      | 4.0                           | null                          | Mismatch           |
      | 406      | null                          | 4.0                           | Mismatch           |

